### Phase 2: New Front-Ends (AGI, SCI, SCUMM)
*(Implement lexer/parser/COPY/CLI/tests for each)*
**AGI** (`src/frontend-agi/` - new directory):
- Lexer: tokenize `.agi` files (line-based, no semicolons); strings `"…"`; keywords `IF`, `ELSE`, `THEN`, `GOSUB`, `GOTO`, `NEWROOM`, `LOADLOGICS`, `RETURN`, `QUIT`, `ASSIGN`, `INCREMENT`, `DECREMENT`, `SET`, `RESET`, `SAID`, `TEST`, `POSN`, `CONTROLLER`, `HAVEKEY`
- Parser:
  - `IF condition THEN stmts ELSE stmts END-IF` → `(:if cond then-stmts else-stmts)`
  - Conditions: `said("…")`, `test(v,op,v)`, `posn(obj,x1,y1,x2,y2)`, `controller(dir)`, `have.key()`, `and`/`or` (via `;` in conditions)
  - `ASSIGN var exp`, `INCR var`, `DECR var` → `(:set var exp)`; `SET flag`/`RESET flag` → `(:set flag true/false)`
  - `NEWROOM n`, `LOADLOGICS n`, `GOSUB name`, `GOTO label` → `(:call-acc :target name)` (far calls via `:bank`; library via `:library t`; object methods via `:invoke`)
  - `RETURN`/`QUIT` → `(:goback)`; `RETURN exp` → `(:goback :using exp)` (accumulator return)
- COPY: `copy("Filename");` → emit `(:copy :name …)` (AGI is line-based; no trailing semicolon needed)
- CLI: `.agi` extension + `-l agi` alias; `compile-agi-from-path` wrapper → `compile-ast-program`
- Tests: FiveAM suite for node shapes, COPY expansion, call forms

**SCI** (`src/frontend-sci/` - new directory):
- Lexer: tokenize `.sci` files (Lisp-like); parentheses `(` `)`; strings `"…"`; keywords `IF`, `WHILE`, `FOR`, `SWITCH`, `CASE`, `DEFAULT`, `BREAK`, `RETURN`, `PROC`, `METHOD`, `CLASS`, `INSTANCE`, `SEND`, `SELF`, `SUPER`, `PRINT`, `SET`, `IF`, `AND`, `OR`, `NOT`, `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `=`
- Parser:
  - `(IF cond expr expr)` / `(ELSE expr)` → `(:if cond then-expr else-expr)`
  - `(WHILE cond body)` → `(:perform :body body :until cond)` (lowered via Phase 0)
  - `(FOR ((= i start)) (< i end) ((++ i)) body)` → `(:perform :body body :varying i :from start :by +1 :until (< i end))`
  - `(SWITCH expr (CASE n body) … (DEFAULT body))` → `(:evaluate :subject expr :when-clauses ((:when (= subject n) body)…) (:when-other body))`
  - `(SET var exp)` → `(:set var exp)`
  - `(+ a b)`, `(- a b)`, `(* a b)`, `(/ a b)` → `(:compute :expression (:add a b))` etc.
  - `(SEND obj method arg)` → `(:invoke :object obj :method method :using arg)` (if arg present)
  - `(SELF method)` → `(:invoke :object self :method method)`
  - `(SUPER method)` → `(:invoke-super :object self :method method)`
  - `(PROC name (params) body)` / `(METHOD name (params) body)` → `(:method name :statements body)` in class context
  - `(CLASS name (slots) body)` / `(INSTANCE name class init)` → class/instance setup (details in implementation)
  - `(PRINT "text")` → `(:call-acc :target "PrintRoutine" :using text-len)` (desugared via sugar layer)
  - `(RETURN exp)` → `(:goback :using exp)`
- COPY: `(copy "Filename")` → emit `(:copy :name …)` (Lisp-style)
- CLI: `.sci` extension + `-l sci` alias; `compile-sci-from-path` wrapper → `compile-ast-program`
- Tests: FiveAM suite for node shapes, COPY expansion, call forms, loop lowering

**SCUMM** (`src/frontend-scumm/` - new directory):
- Lexer: tokenize `.scumm` files (C-like); `{` `}` `[` `]` `(` `)` `;` `,`; strings `"…"`; keywords `if`, `else`, `while`, `do`, `for`, `break`, `continue`, `setState`, `ifState`, `setVar`, `ifVar`, `putActor`, `walkActor`, `loadRoom`, `startScript`, `stopObjectCode`, `print`, `drawSentence`, `setMessage`, `getVar`
- Parser:
  - `if (cond) { } else { }` → `(:if cond then-stmts else-stmts)`
  - `while (cond) { }` → `(:perform :body body :until cond)`
  - `do { } while (cond)` → `(:perform :body body :until cond)` (do-while: body first, then check)
  - `for (init; cond; update) { }` → `(:perform :body body :varying … :from … :by … :until …)` (parses init/cond/update)
  - `break` → `(:break)`; `continue` → `(:continue)`
  - `setState(actor,bit)` / `ifState(actor,bit)` → `(:set :state actor bit)` / `(:if :state actor bit)` (desugared via sugar layer)
  - `setVar(v,n)` / `ifVar(v,op,n)` → `(:set var n)` / `(:if var op n)`
  - `putActor(actor,x,y)` / `walkActor(actor,x,y)` / `loadRoom(n)` / `startScript(n,arg)` → `(:call-acc :target routine :using packed-args)` (desugared via sugar layer)
  - `stopObjectCode()` → `(:goback)`
  - `print "text"` → `(:call-acc :target "PrintRoutine" :using text-len)` (desugared)
- COPY: `copy("Filename");` → emit `(:copy :name …)`
- CLI: `.scumm` extension + `-l scumm` alias; `compile-scumm-from-path` wrapper → `compile-ast-program`
- Tests: FiveAM suite for node shapes, COPY expansion, call forms, loop lowering, break/continue

### Phase 3: Semantic-Sugar / Macro Layer
*(Data-driven desugar pass for Lingo/AGI/SCI/SCUMM)*
- **Purpose**: Map high-level action statements to `:call-acc`/`:invoke`/`:print` of the shared Fountain/Forth runtime library (used by Phantasia's scripting).
- **Implementation**:
  1. After parsing (before optimization), walk the AST for action statements in Lingo/AGI/SCI/SCUMM.
  2. For each recognized action (e.g., `"actor walk to point"`, `"start script"`, `"show message"`), replace with:
     - `(:call-acc :target "LibraryRoutineName" :bank nil :library t :using packed-args)` for calls
     - `(:invoke :object "LibraryObj" :method "MethodName" :using packed-args)` for object methods
     - `(:call-acc :target "PrintRoutine" :using text-len)` for print/display actions
  3. Routine names/bank/service table:
     - Researched from Phantasia's Fountain/Forth scripting runtime at implementation time
     - Stored in one place (e.g., `src/eightbol-compile.lisp` or `src/cobol-copybook.lisp`) so all four front-ends share it
     - Example entries: `"actor walk"` → `(:call-acc :target "WalkActor" :using packed-x-y)`, `"show message"` → `(:call-acc :target "DisplayMessage" :using message-id)`
  4. Ensures no I/O: all outputs (text, graphics, etc.) go through library calls.
- **Languages**: Applied to Lingo, AGI, SCI, SCUMM front-ends only.

### Phase 4: Tests, Documentation & Verification
1. **FiveAM Tests**:
   - Per-front-end: node shapes, COPY expansion, call forms (direct/far/library/object), `:call-acc`/`:returning`, loop lowering (`while`/`for`/`do`), break/continue, sugar-layer desugaring
   - Back-end matrix: smoke-test each front-end × at least one non-6502 CPU (e.g., `:z80`, `:m68k`)
   - CLI test: `bin/eightbol -l agi examples/agi-test.agi -o out.asm` etc.
2. **Documentation Updates**:
   - `doc/EIGHTBOL.texi`: Add chapters for AGI, SCI, SCUMM; update COPY, PERFORM, CLI sections
   - `EIGHTBOLCompiler.texf`: Update `:call-acc` documentation (now real), PERFORM `:body`, COPY expansion
   - `AGENTS.md`: Update supported/unsupported lists (e.g., remove `**` from FORTRAN unsupported if normalized)
3. **Final Verification**:
   - `(asdf:test-system :eightbol)` green via `make test`
   - No unknown kwargs passed to `make-*-node` constructors (grep audit)
   - All front-ends emit only contract-valid AST consumable by back-ends

## Sequencing & Risk Management
- **Safe & Tested**: Each phase ends with `make test` green; Phases are largely independent.
- **Phase Order**: 0 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (Phase 2 depends only on 0; Phase 3 depends on 0 and 2; Phase 4 depends on all).
- **Risks Mitigated**:
  - 13-backend loop codegen: Isolated to Phase 0; each backend updated independently.
  - Runtime routine catalogue (Phase 3): Research task; placeholder table used early; refined during implementation.
  - Three new parsers: Net-new code (~3× front-end dirs); developed incrementally with tests.
  - COBOL `PERFORM…END-PERFORM`: Shares `:body` lowering logic with other loops (no extra work).
- **Exit Criteria**: `make test` passes; all 11 front-ends emit valid AST; all 13 back-ends compile it correctly.

